+# Task 8.6 / Task 3.2 Complete activation independent review
+
+Date: 2026-11-16. Worktree: X:/ocv302. Branch: draft/admit-dag-public-handle-seam. Base: `94e9aca5632bd77d0c6ecde9d7fe689bcdee18d1`. This is the next uncommitted target requested by the owner: the Core.Tests fix, three P3 findings, and five-row Complete promotion. It is not another contract draft and does not claim a new independent contract approval.
+
+The preceding reviewed merge is `1e960fc4bf67ad6d1a8c053602d4a58964b47d79`, ordered parents `598c6d4` then `ba2b057d`, tree `ff4711dca44f7a56abd53bf0854c10332831e814`. Its only evidence child is the base above. That child changes exactly the integration/remediation verdict and the two catalogue/freeze fixtures. The verdict is 12,688 LF bytes, SHA-256 `e9c5feddb651cbb570d289027b6c43b27eebc08b92dec2cd907a784468366074`. Both commits are pushed; neither activates this target.
+
+## Target and findings resolved
+
+- F1: no three 25 ms Task.Delay polls remain. Child entry is a barrier; the redundant snapshot poll is removed; lease retry is explicitly bounded by provider expiry with queued-request cleanup. The Core guard is unchanged and the complete CI unit list passes.
+- F2: current status in CLAUDE and both doc 17 copies names the real approvals. Runtime-view contract approval is no longer misattributed. The compiled integration smoke filter is corrected.
+- F3: missing/incompatible child binding is explicitly host-configuration behavior outside the five seam requirements, as permitted by the verdict. No delta, canonical block, product source or API baseline changes.
+- F4: draft source/document pins now validate committed history. Complete evidence binds real checkpoints and verdict children; the exact current canonical/API/document guards remain. All three shutdown-sync paths require their reviewed after-state; a rollback fails.
+- Task 3.2: promote exactly five registry rows to Complete, update measured provenance, and activate only reshape 8.6. The checkboxes and rows are prepared in this worktree, pending this review. Archival is separate.
+
+## Evidence and review questions
+
+Read the artifacts under `openspec/changes/admit-dag-public-handle-seam/artifacts/`: `task-3-2-owner-authority-2026-11-16.md`, `task-3-2-author-self-review-2026-11-16.md`, `task-3-2-activation-validation-2026-11-16.json`, and `task-3-2-complete-openspec-provenance-2026-11-16.md`.
+
+The validation JSON records fresh Debug/Release rebuilds, all six CI unit projects (1,149 tests), Integration 11, benchmark smoke, nine package consumers, infrastructure/ExpectedRed counters, strict OpenSpec, and scoped mutation results. PostgreSQL and SQL Server rerun the two affected fault/four-process restart cases each; the reviewed merge's full 123/94 provider suites are inherited rather than relabelled as fresh runs. Structural validation is not approval. The five killed mutations and positive historical-scope probe are documented, including restored files and initial failures.
+
+Please verify the exact two-commit chain first, then judge the F1 retry bound and cleanup, the F2/F3 wording, the F4 retirement without loss of current checks, and whether the five-row Complete evidence and task activation faithfully use the actual reviewed scope. The author self-review is not an independent verdict. Earlier reviewers explicitly excluded independent RV-1 through RV-4 contract review; that qualification is retained.
+
+## Freeze and next checkpoint boundary
+
+The self-inclusive raw-order manifest is `developer-facing-interface-section-08-task-8-6-dag-public-handle-seam-task-3-2-complete-activation-dirty-manifest-2026-11-16.txt`. The active content record in `review-manifest-provenance.json` excludes only that self-referential fixture. Review documents are catalogued in immutable history. All earlier packets remain byte-exact. A copied index produces the projected tree; the real index stays untouched. Do not infer an activation checkpoint from the earlier merge/evidence chain.
+
+Leave this target uncommitted until the next independent review. Approval should apply only to this Task 3.2 target; it does not activate another task or archive the change.
